  "finding": "Neither dataset produced a checkpoint more like the target speaker on held-out prompts. V-real degrades acoustically as well as textually - by epoch 4 the median voiced frame count is 0, meaning most generations emit no sound at all. V-tts stays audible but its best arms win on 5 of 10, half the bar.",
  "limits": [
    "ECAPA favours flat, over-smoothed output - the tool's own docstring says so - so these numbers are if anything generous to the degraded arms. The interlock in likeness_guard prevents a degenerate arm passing on them regardless.",
    "The memorisation verdict is not computed here; with this many arms failing on consistency alone it cannot change the outcome.",
    "The target centroid is built from the same 10 recordings that prompt the held-out generations. That is the design M0 and M2 used, and it makes the comparison paired, but it is not an independent sample of the speaker."
  ]
